Third-party notices for مزيج / Mazij Studio
=============================================

This file lists third-party dependencies bundled with the app whose licenses
require attribution. It is scoped to dependencies added alongside this entry;
it does not claim to be an exhaustive audit of every package in package.json.

lottie-web
----------
License: MIT
Copyright (c) 2015 Hernan Torrisi
Used for: importing and playing back Lottie (bodymovin) animations as a real
element on the artboard (roadmap item #13), both in the live editor preview and
when compositing PNG/video export frames.
https://github.com/airbnb/lottie-web

fflate
------
License: MIT
Copyright (c) 2020 Arjun Barrett
Used for: unzipping `.lottie` (dotLottie) animation containers to extract the
embedded animation JSON and any bundled raster image assets.
https://github.com/101arrowz/fflate

harfbuzzjs
----------
License: MIT
Copyright (c) 2019-2026 The harfbuzzjs project authors
(a WebAssembly build of HarfBuzz itself, also MIT-licensed)
Used for: real Arabic text shaping (joining forms, ligatures via GSUB, diacritic/mark
placement via GPOS) and real glyph outline extraction (`Font.glyphToPath`), for the
text paths that need per-glyph control — currently "convert text to outlines"
(roadmap item #12). Plain text elsewhere in the app is left to the platform's own
text engine, which already uses HarfBuzz internally.
https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzzjs

bidi-js
-------
License: MIT
Copyright (c) 2021 Jason Johnston
Used for: the Unicode Bidirectional Algorithm (UAX #9) — resolving paragraph
embedding levels and visual run order for mixed Arabic/Latin/digit text, run
*before* HarfBuzz shaping (roadmap item #12) — see src/lib/arabicShaping.ts.
https://github.com/lojjic/bidi-js

woff2-encoder
-------------
License: MIT
Copyright (c) 2023-present Kyedo
Used for: decompressing this app's bundled `.woff2` font files into raw sfnt bytes
for HarfBuzz (its WASM build has no WOFF2/Brotli decoder of its own) — only the
`/decompress` subpath is imported, for a smaller bundle. (`wawoff2`, the more
commonly cited package for this, was tried first but never completes its WASM
runtime init under Vite/browser ESM — see the comment in `arabicShaping.ts`.)
https://github.com/itskyedo/woff2-encoder
